// Title: New User Account Creation Attempt Via ADSI
// ID: e50d5d26-0cf6-4045-b82b-13c0a4e316be
// Status: experimental
// Level: medium
// Author: William Gokah (idea), Raylee Hawkins, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-08-13
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.t1136.001, attack.t1136.002
// Description: Detects an attempt to create a new user account via ADSI (Active Directory Service Interfaces)
// using either the WinNT or LDAP provider. This is an uncommon method to create user accounts
// and may indicate an attempt to evade detection by avoiding more commonly monitored commands
// such as "net user", "New-LocalUser" or "New-ADUser".
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

from siem.events where ((contains(ScriptBlockText, "[ADSI]")) AND ((contains(ScriptBlockText, "WinNT://") OR contains(ScriptBlockText, "LDAP://"))) AND ((contains(ScriptBlockText, ".create(\"user") OR contains(ScriptBlockText, ".create('user"))))
